    "source_review": [
      "Owned files, modes, patch and complete Reader/ServiceTrace implementations equal495; current read binds this carry, not a full current Voice or native result.",
      "Completion uses a per-instance mpsc receiver. Each reviewed call passes the bounded report from that same writer/state. Report has no identity token; no general cross-writer identity guarantee is claimed for this test-only helper.",
      "After observing closed, writer_loop pops again before EOF, drains accepted packets, finishes/syncs the store and drops owned store/files before the completion send. The writer-failure latch remains visible.",
      "finish and Drop take the producer, store closed with Release and unpark. finish clamps its wait to500ms; Drop never joins or preempts filesystem I/O. The test observer waits2/5s only when bounded finish did not acknowledge, reads final health after the event and never changes the original report.",
      "Packet encoding completes JSON plus newline inside32KiB before enqueueing. Capacity64, four4MiB segments, oversize counters and disk-failure controls remain. A partial regular-file write may fail and latch health; atomic record writes are not promised.",
      "Final-data predicates intentionally inspect the completed report; they do not establish a500ms writer-latency guarantee. The stalled control rechecks the immutable degraded/unacknowledged bounded report after completion. The failed-writer control retains writer_failed.",
      "The Linux test-only pinned root excludes only ancestry above it. Root and downward owner/mode/ACL/component checks remain; the three-way boundary control restores controlled modes before fixture cleanup. These Linux/DAC cases are not selected on Mac.",
      "The selected ten Mac cases use parsing, private SessionDirectory files and writer threads. SessionDirectory::create does not spawn a child. No normal Voice or external process executable is required. The unrelated process fixture exec-marker protocol is not selected."
    ],
